arXiv:2509.19489v1 [cs.AI] 23 Sep 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Estimating the Self-Consistency of LLMs</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Robert Nowak
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>University of Wisconsin-Madison
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p">Systems often repeat the same prompt to large language models (LLMs) and aggregate responses to improve reliability. Common approaches include <em id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">self-consistency</em> or simple majority voting (sample multiple outputs and choose the mode), <em id="p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">prompt ensembling</em> (rephrasing prompts to reduce wording sensitivity), and <em id="p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multi-agent debate</em> (running multiple instances and aggregating their conclusions). Such consensus methods can stabilize outputs and improve accuracy, especially on multi-step reasoning tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>. This short note analyzes an estimator of the self-consistency of LLMs and the tradeoffs it induces under a fixed compute budget <math id="p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=mn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=mn</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of prompts sampled from the task distribution and <math id="p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of repeated LLM calls per prompt; the resulting analysis favors a rough split <math id="p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,n\propto\sqrt{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,n\propto\sqrt{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. It complements recent work on self-consistency prompting that aggregates multiple sampled reasoning paths to stabilize predictions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a prompt <math id="p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> that requires a binary response. Suppose we call an LLM <math id="p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> times to ask if this is a positive or negative <math id="p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Our analysis concerns <em id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">self-consistency error</em>. Assume the <math id="p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> responses are independent and identically distributed and let <math id="p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability of a positive response. The self-consistency error of the LLM on <math id="p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S0.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal E}(x)=\min\{p(x),1-p(x)\}\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal E}(x)=\min\{p(x),1-p(x)\}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p2.2" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, taking the model’s most probable label as the reference, <math id="p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal E}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal E}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability that an independently sampled response disagrees with that (majority) label.</p>
</div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p3.1" class="ltx_p">The average self-consistency error over a domain of prompts <math id="p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S0.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal E}\ :=\ \frac{1}{|{\mathcal{X}}|}\sum_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}{\cal E}(x)\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal E}\ :=\ \frac{1}{|{\mathcal{X}}|}\sum_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}{\cal E}(x)\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p3.2" class="ltx_p">Instead of the uniform distribution of <math id="p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can also consider a general distribution <math id="p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In that case, the
average self-consistency error rate over a domain of prompts <math id="p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined to be</p>
<table id="S0.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal E}\ :=\ \sum_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}{\cal E}(x)\,q(x)\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal E}\ :=\ \sum_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}{\cal E}(x)\,q(x)\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p4.1" class="ltx_p">To estimate the self-consistency error for a given <math id="p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> consider the plug-in estimator based on <math id="p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{p}(x)=k/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{p}(x)=k/n</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of calls to the LLM that come back positive,</p>
<table id="S0.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cal E}(x)\ :=\ \min\{k/n,1-k/n\}\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cal E}(x)\ :=\ \min\{k/n,1-k/n\}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p4.2" class="ltx_p">The average error can be estimated by drawing <math id="p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> prompts <math id="p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> independently according to the distribution <math id="p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> (possibly uniform) from <math id="p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and forming the estimator</p>
<table id="S0.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cal E}\ :=\ \frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cal E}\ :=\ \frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected squared error of the estimator <math id="Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cal E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cal E}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the bound</span></p>
<table id="S0.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]\ \leq\ \frac{1}{8m}+\frac{1}{\pi n}+\frac{1}{2nm}\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]\ \leq\ \frac{1}{8m}+\frac{1}{\pi n}+\frac{1}{2nm}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p5.1" class="ltx_p">The first term is due to the variance incurred by the random subsample of prompts used to form the estimator. The second term is due to the bias inherent in the estimator <math id="p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cal E}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cal E}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and the third term is due to its variance. The theorem suggests that given a budget <math id="p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> of total calls to the LLM, the upper bound is minimized by taking <math id="p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=n=O(\sqrt{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=n=O(\sqrt{B})</annotation></semantics></math> (since the third term in the bound is negligible compared to the other two terms). The upper bound is exactly minimized by</p>
<table id="S0.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}\;=\;\sqrt{\tfrac{\pi B}{8}},\qquad n^{*}\;=\;\sqrt{\tfrac{8B}{\pi}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}\;=\;\sqrt{\tfrac{\pi B}{8}},\qquad n^{*}\;=\;\sqrt{\tfrac{8B}{\pi}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p5.2" class="ltx_p">and these real values can be rounded to the nearest integers.</p>
</div>
<div id="id1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume that <math id="p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even and that <math id="p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=p(x)\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=p(x)\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>; similar derivations can be carried out when <math id="p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is odd and/or <math id="p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)&gt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)&gt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. To bound the bias of <math id="p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cal E}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cal E}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> first note that the expectation of <math id="p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\,\widehat{\cal E}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\,\widehat{\cal E}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\min\{k,n-k\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[\min\{k,n-k\}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n/2}k\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}\ +\ \sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(n-k)\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n/2}k\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}\ +\ \sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(n-k)\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n}k\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}\ +\ \sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(n-2k)\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n}k\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}\ +\ \sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(n-2k)\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle np\ +\ \sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(n-2k)\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle np\ +\ \sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(n-2k)\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">So the bias is given by</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\cal E}(x)-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\cal E}(x)-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(2k-n)\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}\ \geq\ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(2k-n)\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}\ \geq\ 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Next we upper bound the bias. The bound that follows is probably known, but a good reference was not found, so the derivation is included here.
First note that bias is largest when <math id="p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=1/2</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;n/2</annotation></semantics></math> in the sum. So we have the bound</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\cal E}(x)-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\cal E}(x)-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(2k-n)\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}(2k-n)\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">The mean of a binomial distribution with parameters <math id="p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math>, and by symmetry <math id="p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}k\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}=\sum_{k=1}{n/2}k\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}=n/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}k\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}=\sum_{k=1}{n/2}k\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}=n/4</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="S0.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}2k\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}=1/2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}2k\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}=1/2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Next consider</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{n/2+1}^{n}\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{n/2}^{n}\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}-\frac{1}{2}\binom{n}{n/2}2^{-n}\ =\ 1/2-\frac{1}{2}\binom{n}{n/2}2^{-n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{n/2}^{n}\binom{n}{k}2^{-n}-\frac{1}{2}\binom{n}{n/2}2^{-n}\ =\ 1/2-\frac{1}{2}\binom{n}{n/2}2^{-n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">Combining this with the previous bound, we have</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\cal E}(x)-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\cal E}(x)-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\binom{n}{n/2}2^{-n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\binom{n}{n/2}2^{-n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.7.1" class="ltx_text">This can be further bounded using upper and lower bounds to Stirling’s approximation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>. Applying these bounds we have</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\binom{n}{n/2}2^{-n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\binom{n}{n/2}2^{-n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2^{-n}\frac{\sqrt{2\pi n}(n/e)^{n}e^{\frac{1}{12n}}}{(\sqrt{2\pi n/2}((n/2)/e)^{n/2}e^{\frac{1}{6n+1}})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2^{-n}\frac{\sqrt{2\pi n}(n/e)^{n}e^{\frac{1}{12n}}}{(\sqrt{2\pi n/2}((n/2)/e)^{n/2}e^{\frac{1}{6n+1}})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi n}}e^{\frac{1}{12n}-\frac{2}{6n+1}}\ \leq\ \sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi n}}e^{\frac{1}{12n}-\frac{2}{6n+1}}\ \leq\ \sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.8.1" class="ltx_text">This yields the bound</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\cal E}(x)-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\cal E}(x)-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\frac{1}{2\pi n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\frac{1}{2\pi n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.9.1" class="ltx_text">We can bound the variance of <math id="p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cal E}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cal E}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> using the fact that <math id="p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\{p,1-p\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\{p,1-p\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <span id="p6.9.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz</span> function in <math id="p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{V}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]\ =\ {\mathbb{V}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)-{\cal E}(x)]\ \leq\ {\mathbb{E}}[(\widehat{\cal E}(x)-{\cal E}(x))^{2}]\ \leq\ {\mathbb{E}}[(\widehat{p}(x)-p(x))^{2}]\ \leq\ \frac{1}{4n}\ ." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{V}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)]\ =\ {\mathbb{V}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x)-{\cal E}(x)]\ \leq\ {\mathbb{E}}[(\widehat{\cal E}(x)-{\cal E}(x))^{2}]\ \leq\ {\mathbb{E}}[(\widehat{p}(x)-p(x))^{2}]\ \leq\ \frac{1}{4n}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.10.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider estimating the overall probability of error <math id="p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal E}:=\sum_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}{\cal E}(x)\,q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal E}:=\sum_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}{\cal E}(x)\,q(x)</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn independently according to the distribution <math id="p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cal E}:=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cal E}:=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\cal E}:=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\cal E}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\cal E}:=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\cal E}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The expected squared error of this estimator is bounded as follows.</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\tilde{\cal E}+\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\tilde{\cal E}+\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\tilde{\cal E})^{2}]+2\,{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\tilde{\cal E})^{2}]+2\,{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{8m}+2\,{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]\ ," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{8m}+2\,{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]\ ,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.11.1" class="ltx_text">where we use the fact that <math id="p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\cal E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\cal E}</annotation></semantics></math> is an unbiased estimator of <math id="p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal E}</annotation></semantics></math> and it is the average of <math id="p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> random variables in <math id="p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1/2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1/2]</annotation></semantics></math>; thus, its variance is at most <math id="p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{16m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{16m}</annotation></semantics></math>. We next bound <math id="p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{m^{2}}{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\cal E}(x_{i})-\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})\Big)^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{m^{2}}{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\cal E}(x_{i})-\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})\Big)^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{m^{2}}{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\cal E}(x_{i})-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})]+{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})]-\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})\Big)^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{m^{2}}{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\cal E}(x_{i})-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})]+{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})]-\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})\Big)^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.12.1" class="ltx_text">To simplify the notation, let <math id="p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}={\cal E}(x_{i})-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}={\cal E}(x_{i})-{\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}={\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})]-\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}={\mathbb{E}}[\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})]-\widehat{\cal E}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="p6.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,m</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[(\tilde{\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{m^{2}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{m}{\mathbb{E}}[(a_{i}+b_{i})(a_{j}+b_{j})]\ =\ \frac{1}{m^{2}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{m}{\mathbb{E}}[a_{i}a_{j}]+\frac{1}{m^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\mathbb{E}}[b_{i}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{m^{2}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{m}{\mathbb{E}}[(a_{i}+b_{i})(a_{j}+b_{j})]\ =\ \frac{1}{m^{2}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{m}{\mathbb{E}}[a_{i}a_{j}]+\frac{1}{m^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\mathbb{E}}[b_{i}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2\pi n}+\frac{1}{4nm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2\pi n}+\frac{1}{4nm}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.13.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="p6.m31" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[a_{i}b_{j}]={\mathbb{E}}[a_{i}{\mathbb{E}}[b_{j}|x_{1},\dots,x_{m}]]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[a_{i}b_{j}]={\mathbb{E}}[a_{i}{\mathbb{E}}[b_{j}|x_{1},\dots,x_{m}]]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="p6.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="p6.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}[b_{i}^{2}]\leq\frac{1}{4n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}[b_{i}^{2}]\leq\frac{1}{4n}</annotation></semantics></math>. So we have</span></p>
<table id="S0.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S0.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}[({\cal E}-\widehat{\cal E})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S0.Ex27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{8m}+\frac{1}{\pi n}+\frac{1}{2nm}\ ." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{8m}+\frac{1}{\pi n}+\frac{1}{2nm}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="p6.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="p6.14.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Possible Extensions.</h2>

<div id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond the mean-squared analysis of the binary self-consistency error, one can (i) derive <em id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">high-probability</em> bounds by combining Bernstein (for <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\cal E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\cal E}</annotation></semantics></math>) with binomial concentration for <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\cal E}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\cal E}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and a union bound over <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>; (ii) extend to <em id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multi-class</em> settings by replacing <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal E}(x)=\min\{p,1-p\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal E}(x)=\min\{p,1-p\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal E}(x)=1-\max_{c}p_{c}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal E}(x)=1-\max_{c}p_{c}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding analogous <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/m</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/n</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/(mn)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/(mn)</annotation></semantics></math> scalings up to constants; and (iii) model correlated LLM calls via an intraclass correlation <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, inflating the variance term and quantifying the erosion of majority-vote gains. These refinements preserve the optimal budget split <math id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*},\,n^{*}\propto\sqrt{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*},\,n^{*}\propto\sqrt{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and clarify when departures from iid  sampling (e.g., shared randomness, caching) impact the constants.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Acknowledgment.</h2>

<div id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S0.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work was partially supported by NSF AI-EDGE Institute (NSF Award 2112471).</p>
</div>
</section>
